CI/CD Classic to YAML Migration Checklist
1. Trigger & Repository Info
[ ] Repository type and URL (Azure Repos, GitHub, etc.)
[ ] Branch filters for CI/CD trigger
[ ] Path filters (include/exclude folders/files)
[ ] Pull Request triggers
[ ] Scheduled triggers (CRON or interval-based)
2. Variables
[ ] Pipeline-level variables
[ ] Secret variables
[ ] Variable groups (including Azure Key Vault references)
[ ] Environment-specific variable overrides
3. Build Pipeline Tasks
[ ] Task name and type (e.g., .NET build, npm install)
[ ] Task input parameters (e.g., arguments, file paths)
[ ] Execution order of tasks
[ ] Custom scripts (PowerShell, Bash, CMD)
[ ] Task conditions (run on success/failure/etc.)
[ ] Agent pool and specification (e.g., windows-latest)
4. Artifacts
[ ] Artifact names and paths
[ ] Artifact publish location
[ ] Artifact usage in release pipeline
5. Release Pipeline Info
[ ] Release stages (e.g., QA, Staging, Production)
[ ] Deployment tasks per stage
[ ] Stage-specific variables/configurations
6. Environments & Approvals
[ ] Defined environments
[ ] Pre-deployment approvals (user/group)
[ ] Post-deployment approvals
[ ] Gates (delay, query checks, etc.)
7. Service Connections
[ ] Azure, Docker Hub, GitHub, or other service connections
[ ] Connection names and scopes
8. Retention, Notifications, and Other Settings
[ ] Retention policies
[ ] Pipeline notification rules
[ ] Build tags
[ ] Branch policies linked to pipeline
9. Security & Access
[ ] Approval permissions (who can approve)
[ ] Pipeline-level security settings
